            <ArticleTitle>Transient global brainstem dysfunction after microvascular decompression of the trigeminal nerve.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>275-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Microvascular decompression of the trigeminal nerve root entry zone has become a standard treatment for trigeminal neuralgia. It has been widely reported with a low morbidity. This case report details an unusual and previously unreported complication of this procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
